          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            %em congruence
            one means the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            on the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            which regards two of these as equivalent if one is carried into the other by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            (of the ambient Euclidean space).
          %p
            Similarly, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %em congruence
            one means certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relations"} equivalence relations
            on elements of algebraic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
            (cf. e.g. the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group+of+integers+modulo+n"} multiplicative group of integers modulo n
          %p
            Therefore, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            the term
            %em congruence
            is used in the broad generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relations"} equivalence relations
            on (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
            of)
            %em any object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
            %em any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
