            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %strong congruence
              on an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (i.e.: an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
              — hence an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
              with all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              — but with no non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            %p
              This means that it consists of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            #eq:TheSubobject.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i
                    \\;\colon\;
                    R\stackrel{(p_1,p_2)}\hookrightarrow X \times X
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with itself, equipped with the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  internal
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexivity
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \colon X \to R
                  which is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  both of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
                  and of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mi r
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mi r
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1 r = p_2 r = 1_X
              %li
                %p
                  internal
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetry
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \colon R \to R
                  which interchanges
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1\circ s = p_2
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi s
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2\circ s = p_1
              %li#InternalTransitivity
                %p
                  internal
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitivity
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \,\colon\, R \times_X R \to R
                %p
                  (where on the left we have the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \hookrightarrow X \times X \overset{p_2}{\to} X
                  with
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mn 1
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \hookrightarrow X \times X \overset{p_1}{\to} X
                  %em composable
                  pairs in relation)
                %p
                  which factors the left/right projection map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \times_X R \to X \times X
                  through
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi t
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                                %msub
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi X
                                %mi R
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 1
                                    %msub
                                      %mi q
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo ,
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 2
                                    %msub
                                      %mi q
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; R
                        \\\
                        \&amp;
                        {}^{\mathllap{t}}\nearrow
                        \&amp;
                        \\big\downarrow
                        \\\
                        R \times_X R
                        \&amp;
                        \\underset{(p_1 q_1,p_2 q_2)}{\longrightarrow}
                        \&amp;
                        X \times X
                        \\mathrlap{\,,}
                        }
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_1
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_2
                  are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
                  defined by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback diagram
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                                %msub
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mi X
                                %mi R
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi q
                                      %mn 2
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mrow
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi q
                                          %mn 1
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mrow
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi p
                                          %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi R
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mn 2
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        R \times_X R
                        \&amp;
                        \\overset{q_2}\longrightarrow
                        \&amp;
                        R
                        \\\
                        \\big\downarrow{\mathrlap{{}^{q_1}}}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\big\downarrow{\mathrlap{{}^{p_1}}}
                        \\\
                        R
                        \&amp;
                        \\underset{p_2}\longrightarrow
                        \&amp;
                        X
                        }
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              are necessarily unique if they exist.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Equivalently, a congruence on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the object of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              and such that if there is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \to x_2
              then there is also a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2 \to x_1
              (internally).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              We can equivalently define a congruence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              as (a representing object of) a representable sub-presheaf of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, X \times X)
              so that for each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(Y) \hookrightarrow \hom(Y, X \times X) \cong \hom(Y, X) \times \hom(Y, X)
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(Y)
              as an equivalence relation on the set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(Y, X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is not finitely complete.
          #EffectiveCongruence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A congruence which is the kernel pair of some morphism (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KernelPairIsCongruence"}
              = succeed "." do
                %strong effective
          #QuotientObject.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              of a congruence is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient object
            %p
              The quotient of an effective congruence is called an
              = succeed "." do
                %strong effective quotient
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
              is called an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
              if every congruence is effective.
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              An effective congruence, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EffectiveCongruence"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              of its quotient, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuotientObject"}
          %h2#examples Examples
          #DiagonalMorphismIsCongruence.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+morphism"} diagonal morphism
              on an object is a congruence and has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
              to the original object.
          #KernelPairIsCongruence.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              is a congruence.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              is precisely a congruence in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The eponymous example is congruence modulo
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (for a fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              in the category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigs"} rigs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              in the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \hookrightarrow G
              is the quotient of the congruence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msup
                        %mi y
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \{(x,y) : x y^{-1} \in K \}
            %p
              Alternatively, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \hookrightarrow G
              is the quotient of the congruence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi K
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times K \stackrel{(p_1,p_2)}{\hookrightarrow} G \times G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
              is projection on the first factor and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
              is multiplication in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              (these are source and target maps in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ⫽
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \sslash K
            %p
              A special case of this is that of a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+module"} quotient module
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The notions of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact category
                can naturally be formulated in terms of congruences. A “higher arity” version, corresponding to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+categories"} coherent categories
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretoposes"} pretoposes
                is discussed at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/familial+regularity+and+exactness"} familial regularity and exactness
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mal%27cev+category"} Mal'cev category
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
                in which every internal relation satisfying reflexivity is thereby actually a congruence.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} Higher-categorical
                generalizations are that of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-congruence"} 2-congruence
                and of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} groupoid object in an (∞,1)-category
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-congruence"} (n,r)-congruence
